**Properties of a cylinder**

**fig-01.** A cylinder drawn upright: an ellipse for the top face, two vertical sides
falling from its ends, and a curve closing the base.

\begin{center}
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.55,line width=0.5pt]
  \draw (-1.2,2.6) arc (180:-180:1.2 and 0.35);
  \draw (-1.2,2.6) -- (-1.2,0);
  \draw (1.2,2.6) -- (1.2,0);
  \draw (-1.2,0) arc (180:360:1.2 and 0.35);
  \draw[dashed] (-1.2,0) arc (180:0:1.2 and 0.35);
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{center}

1. It has two circular faces and one curved face
2. It has no vertex
3. It has two curved edges
4. It has three faces altogether

**Properties of sphere**

**fig-02.** A sphere drawn as a circle with an ellipse across its middle to show the
curved surface.

\begin{center}
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.55,line width=0.5pt]
  \draw (0,0) circle (1.3);
  \draw (-1.3,0) arc (180:360:1.3 and 0.42);
  \draw[dashed] (-1.3,0) arc (180:0:1.3 and 0.42);
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{center}

1. A sphere is symmetrical from all direction
2. It has no edge and no vertex
3. It has one curved surface

**Volume of prism**

Calculate the volume of the prism below.

**fig-03.** A triangular prism lying on its rectangular face. The triangular end has a base
of 5 m and a height of 3 m, and the prism runs back 10 m.

\begin{center}
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.42,line width=0.5pt]
  \draw (0,0) -- (5,0) -- (2.5,3) -- cycle;
  \draw (5,0) -- (8.5,1.8);
  \draw (2.5,3) -- (6,4.8);
  \draw (8.5,1.8) -- (6,4.8);
  \draw[dashed] (0,0) -- (3.5,1.8);
  \draw[dashed] (3.5,1.8) -- (8.5,1.8);
  \draw[dashed] (3.5,1.8) -- (6,4.8);
  \draw[dashed] (2.5,0) -- (2.5,3);
  \node[below] at (2.5,-0.15) {$5\,\mathrm{m}$};
  \node[left] at (2.35,1.5) {$3\,\mathrm{m}$};
  \node[below right] at (6.9,0.8) {$10\,\mathrm{m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{center}

Solution:

Area of triangular face $= \frac{1}{2}bh$

$= \frac{1}{2} \times 5 \times 3$

$= 7.5m^{2}$

Volume of prism $=$ Area of base $\times$ height

$= 7.5m^{2} \times 10m$

$= 75m^{3}$

