steps.note:
**Procedure:**

1. Draw a line segment $AB$ and mark a point $O$ on it where the right angle is to stand.
2. With centre $O$ and any convenient radius, draw an arc to cut $AB$ at $X$ and $Y$.
3. With centre $X$ and a radius greater than $XO$, draw an arc above $AB$.
4. With centre $Y$ and the same radius as in (3), draw an arc to cut the first arc at $Z$.
5. Join $OZ$. Then $\angle ZOA = \angle ZOB = 90^\circ$.

**fig-13.** The line $AB$ with a stroke at each end, the two arc cuts $X$ and $Y$ marked either
side of the middle, and the perpendicular $OZ$ erected from $O$ between them, with a right-angle
mark at its foot and the two arcs crossing at $Z$ near its top.

\begin{center}
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.55,line width=0.5pt]
  \draw (0,0) -- (7,0);
  \draw (0,0.22) -- (0,-0.22);
  \draw (7,0.22) -- (7,-0.22);
  \node[below left] at (0,-0.1) {$A$};
  \node[below right] at (7,-0.1) {$B$};
  \draw (0.29,0.22) -- (0.29,-0.22);
  \draw (0.84,0.34) -- (0.84,-0.34);
  \node[below] at (0.84,-0.38) {$X$};
  \draw (6.13,0.22) -- (6.13,-0.22);
  \node[below] at (6.13,-0.26) {$Y$};
  \draw (6.60,0.34) -- (6.60,-0.34);
  \draw (3.8,0) -- (3.8,3.2);
  \node[below] at (3.8,-0.12) {$O$};
  \draw (4.12,0) -- (4.12,0.32) -- (3.8,0.32);
  \draw (2.9,2.55) -- (4.7,3.05);
  \draw (2.9,3.05) -- (4.7,2.55);
  \node[above right] at (3.8,2.82) {$Z$};
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{center}

